course: dictionary
lesson: 186
title: Ain't and the full form
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ain is not a word on its own. It is the first part of «ain't», a short form with an apostrophe at the end. Check the context to see what «ain't» is doing in the sentence.
explain: Ain't means am not, is not, are not, has not or have not. So «I ain't got any» means «I have not got any», and «it ain't fair» means «it is not fair».
explain: Ain't is informal. People use it when they talk casually, roughly or in a certain place, and authors use it to show how a character speaks. Ask yourself what the speaker sounds like before you decide what the sentence means.
explain: In school writing and exams, write the full form instead. Write «I have not got any» and «it is not fair», not the short form.
fact: Ain't means am not, is not, are not, has not or have not.
fact: Ain't is informal, so write the full form in school work and exams.
fact: Phrases like «it ain't fair» and «if it ain't broke, don't fix it» show how people speak casually.
fact: In French, «ain» is spelt in words like «le pain» (bread), «le vin» (wine) and «la main» (hand), and it makes a nasal sound, a bit like «an» in «cat» sent up the nose.
fact: Ain Jalut is a place name: the Mongols lost a battle there in 1260.
exercise: «I ain't got any pencils.» Which full form could replace ain't here? | does not | is not got | was not | *have not
exercise: In school writing, what should you write instead of «it ain't fair»? | It ain fair | *It is not fair | It aint fair | It ain't fair
exercise: Ain is the first part of which short form? | isn't | won't | don't | *ain't
test: In «the Mongols also lost at Ain Jalut in 1260», what is Ain Jalut? | An informal word for am not | *A place where a battle was fought | A French word for bread | A kind of storm
test: Which sentence is written correctly for school? | I ain going. | I ain't going. | I aint going. | *I am not going.
exam: The saying «if it ain't broke, don't fix it» should be written for school as: | If it ain broke, don fix it. | If it ain't broke, don't fix it. | If it aint broke, dont fix it. | *If it is not broken, do not fix it.
